{"content":"Perfect! Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile the answer:\n\nq29.\n\n**Frontend auth interceptor location:** `web/src/connect.ts` (lines 156–178, the `authInterceptor` constant)\n\n**Tokens managed:**\n1. **Access Token (JWT)** — Short-lived token (15 minutes), managed in `web/src/auth-state.ts`; stored in localStorage under key `\"memos_access_token\"` with expiry in `\"memos_token_expires_at\"`. The interceptor attaches it as a Bearer token in the `Authorization` header.\n2. **Refresh Token (HTTP cookie)** — Long-lived token (30 days), sent automatically via `credentials: \"include\"` (line 60); the interceptor uses `/api/v1/auth/refresh` to get new access tokens.\n3. **Personal Access Token (PAT)** — Prefix `\"memos_pat_\"`, also sent as Bearer token in Authorization header.\n\n**Backend validation package:** `server/auth` (path: `server/auth/authenticator.go`)\n\nThe `Authenticator` struct in `server/auth` provides three validation methods:\n- `AuthenticateByAccessTokenV2()` — validates JWT access tokens via signature only (stateless, lines 39–58)\n- `AuthenticateByRefreshToken()` — validates refresh tokens against the database for revocation checks (lines 60–99)\n- `AuthenticateByPAT()` — validates Personal Access Tokens (lines 101–124)","iteration":9,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
